<title>USA: CCC says buys 11,600 tonnes wheat for Ghana, Benin.</title>
<headline>CCC says buys 11,600 tonnes wheat for Ghana, Benin.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp of the U.S. Department of Agriculture said it bought 10,000 tonnes of northern spring wheat for donation to Ghana and 1,600 tonnes of hard red winter wheat for Benin.</p>
<p>The spring wheat was priced at $171.39 a tonne while the HRW wheat was priced at $172.33, both FOB Paulina.</p>
<p>Peavey Co sold all the wheat for December 1-25 delivery.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
</text>
